Troubleshooting Tips
Issue: "ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'dotenv'"
Solution:

pip3 install python-dotenv --user
Issue: Environment variables not loading
Solution:

# Check .env file exists in the same directory
ls -la .env

# Verify .env file format (no spaces around =)
cat .env

# Ensure load_dotenv() is called before accessing variables
Issue: Permission denied on .env file
Solution:

# Fix permissions
chmod 600 .env

# Verify ownership
ls -la .env
Issue: Variables showing as None
Solution:

# Add debug output in your script
print(f"Current directory: {os.getcwd()}")
print(f".env exists: {os.path.exists('.env')}")
